      "body": "## Summary\n`random-mm`'s synthetic video generator hardcodes the MP4 container encode rate at 30fps (`generate_synthetic_video`), so `--random-mm-bucket-config`'s `num_frames` does not reliably map to the frame count a target model actually processes — that depends on the model's own video preprocessing (e.g. duration-based resampling at its own native fps).\n\nAdds `--random-mm-video-encode-fps` so the encode rate can be set to match a target model's native fps, making `num_frames` self-consistent. Backward compatible: defaults to 30.0 (the previous hardcoded value).\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Syntax/diff reviewed\n- [x] End-to-end test against a running server: `XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-MOPD`, vLLM, TP2, ROCm (MI350-class). Ran `vllm bench serve --dataset-name random-mm --random-mm-bucket-config '{(768,1024,16): 1.0}' --random-mm-limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"video\":1}' --random-mm-video-encode-fps 1.0` against a live server — **4/4 successful requests**.\n",
